Experience Monitoring (VAPT) — production ops

Full guide: deploy/experience-monitoring-production.md
Always run from: /var/www/vendorpulse  (NOT /var/www/exportdoc)

---

Quick deploy

cd /var/www/vendorpulse
git pull
docker compose build --no-cache horizon
docker compose up -d app horizon scheduler
docker compose exec app php artisan config:clear
docker compose exec app php artisan route:clear
docker compose exec horizon npx playwright --version

Then trigger a test from the dashboard and confirm the screenshot loads.

---

When monitoring does not work

Rebuild horizon (Playwright is in that image):

cd /var/www/vendorpulse
docker compose build --no-cache horizon
docker compose up -d app horizon scheduler

Check containers are up:

docker compose ps

Check scheduler logs:

docker compose logs scheduler --tail=20

Check horizon status + failed jobs:

docker compose exec app php artisan horizon:status
docker compose exec app php artisan queue:failed

Follow horizon logs:

docker compose logs -f horizon --tail=50

Install Playwright inside horizon if missing:

docker compose exec horizon npm run experience-monitoring:install
docker compose exec horizon npm run experience-monitoring:verify

.env: do NOT set EXPERIENCE_MONITORING_RUNNER_COMMAND to a host nvm path inside Docker.
Use default `node` (unset the variable) or:

docker compose exec horizon which node

---

Screenshot 404 / not visible

app + horizon must share vendorpulse_storage volume (docker-compose.yml).

After compose change:

cd /var/www/vendorpulse
docker compose up -d app horizon

Verify both containers see the same files:

docker compose exec horizon ls -la storage/app/experience-monitoring/screenshots/
docker compose exec app ls -la storage/app/experience-monitoring/screenshots/

Re-run the VAPT test from the dashboard (old runs may have DB rows but missing files).

---

Fix old firefox/webkit tests (optional)

docker compose exec app php artisan tinker --execute="
\App\Models\ExperienceMonitoringTest::whereIn('browser_type', ['firefox','webkit'])->update(['browser_type' => 'chromium']);
"

---

Check last test result (CLI)

docker compose exec app php artisan tinker --execute="
\$t = \App\Models\ExperienceMonitoringTest::latest()->first();
echo \$t?->name.' last='.\$t?->last_status.' at='.\$t?->last_run_at;
"

---

js_error status

Playwright succeeded; target page logged console.error (often ExportDoc 404/Vite/API).
See run History → browser logs / failed requests in the dashboard.
Login can succeed while status is js_error.

---

Port 8001 (when 8000 is taken by ExportDoc)

In /var/www/vendorpulse/.env:
  APP_PORT=8001
  APP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001

In web_dashboard/.env.local:
  NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1

Then:

cd /var/www/vendorpulse
docker compose up -d --build app horizon scheduler

API: http://127.0.0.1:8001/api/v1

